  "scientific_findings": [
    "Two strong sampled-stationary central features are directly represented in the new saved data: 2303.3203125MHz in native170 and 2297.4609375MHz in native172. Each is selected as rank1 in all three ON lists, with identical six-scan fixed profile records across its three selection instances. These six instances represent two sampled geometries, not six independent sources.",
    "The strongest new native-center profiles have large positive residual means in all ON and OFF scans. They establish no source-specific sky or SETI qualification. The report preserves the full OFF values and their two half-windows.",
    "All 120 existing batch02 top20 originating width boxes intersect the corresponding native-center channel in at least one originating row. This independently derived saved-geometry fact explains why the high-score lists cannot be treated as 120 unrelated strong signals, but it provides no causal classification or calibrated significance.",
    "Many adjacent selected drift tracks have large origin residuals concentrated in one half-window, with rounded width boxes crossing the native-center feature. Such selection-conditioned crossings do not independently validate the fitted drift as a physical trajectory.",
    "Nine selected instances have both half means positive in all three ON scans; seven also have both halves positive in at least one OFF. These signs are descriptive summaries of all preserved profiles, not a new candidate gate or qualified veto.",
    "The known prior native171 feature at 2300.390625MHz is earlier context. The spacing between the three geometric chunk centers is 2.9296875MHz. The new features are observed in their own saved data; equal grid spacing alone establishes neither spill nor an instrumental or astronomical cause.",
    "The 54 profiles and 360 top20 entries remain separate selections within six administrative jobs and three ON origins. Robust maximized scores are not calibrated SNR or FAP; template combinations are correlated.",
    "Full-native raw float32 row medians precede float64 profile promotion. These signed dimensionless profile residuals differ from detector core row-MAD-normalized ranking scores and from joined-boundary normalization."
  ],
